Description of Operations

Alarm – dismiss(String status): Void
This operation allows the ranger to turn off an active alarm after an alert is received. The status parameter keeps track of the status of the alarm when it is turned off. Once the alarm is turned off, it will stay off until another noise is detected at a different location.

Alerts – summary(String status, int time): Void
This operation creates a summary of alerts based on their status and a certain time period. The status can be definite, suspected, or false, and the time is used to determine which alerts should be included.

Alerts – summary(String status): Void
This operation creates a summary based on the status of the alerts. This allows the ranger to see detections that were classified as definite, suspected, or false.

Alerts – summary(int sensor): Void
This operation creates a summary for a specific sensor. The sensor number is used to find and show the detections that came from that sensor location.

Alerts – summaryMap(): Void
This operation creates a map showing where detections happened. It allows the ranger to see the detections around the park and the areas within two miles of the park.

Alerts – summaryRanger(int id): Void
This operation creates a summary based on a specific ranger. The ranger's ID is used to show the detection classifications that were made by that ranger.

Classes Without Operations

Sensor
The Sensor keeps track of information coming from each sensor in the park. It contains outgoing: Report, id: Int, and targets: Vector<Animal>. The ID identifies the sensor, targets keeps track of the animals it is looking for, and outgoing is the report being sent from the sensor.

Noise
The Noise class stores information about a noise that was detected. It contains strength: Float, type: Animal, xPos: Float, and zPos: Float. This keeps track of how strong the noise was, what type of animal caused it, and the location where it was detected.

Report
The Report class stores the information collected from a detection. It contains time: Int, sensorID: Int, and noise: Noise. This connects the detected noise to the sensor that detected it and the time it happened.

FiledReport
The FiledReport class stores a report after it has been reviewed. It contains report: Report, status: String, and ranger: *Ranger. The status keeps track of how the detection was classified, and ranger keeps track of which ranger reviewed it.

Ranger
The Ranger class represents a park ranger using the system. It contains name: String and id: Int, which allows each ranger to be identified and connected to the reports they review.

Animal
The Animal class represents the type of animal being detected by the system. The current UML does not show any specific attributes or operations inside this class.

Device
The Device represents the software used by the animal detection device. The UML notes that the device software is designed by Animals-R-Here and is being approximated in this system.

Computer
The Computer represents the controlling computer located at the ranger station. It is connected to the Alarm and Alerts parts of the system and is used to receive and manage the information coming from the sensors.
